Z||000000||DXR_DAD||08-18-2000||12:49 AM||||Has anyone found any way or any thing to replace the clear plastic lens that covers the dash cluster/gauges?? Can you still get this part from GM? Thanks for any help!!<P>DXR_DAD||||reg||5
Z||000001||Oreif||08-18-2000||01:01 AM||||GM doesn't have them. Mine were slightly scuffed and the pod gage one looked a little "cloudy". I just took Meguires plastic polish and sat down and buffed them for an hour each. (while watching a DVD movie) and they came out looking better than new! The trick is put a little on a lint free cloth and buff until the cloth is dry and repeat. My dash one came out looking like glass. (polish on, polish off, polish on, polish off, Good little gwass hopper)  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||DXR_DAD||08-18-2000||01:49 AM||||Thanks oreif<BR>The aux gauge lens looks easy to replace, but the gauge cluster ???? I have a big crack in it ??? Thanks for any help!!!||||reg||5
Z||000003||Bruce||08-18-2000||02:02 AM||||Bill,<BR>There used to be a place right on the Daly City-SF border called "TapPlastics," I think. You just took in what you wanted duplicated, and they did it. You might want to give them a try, unless you're in to DVD's and McGuires.<BR>bb||||reg||1
Z||000004||Oreif||08-18-2000||02:07 AM||||DAD! I have the gage cluster (speedo/tach) from my original dash. (went to a 120mph dash) The only problem with it is a crack by the mounting screw just above the odometer. The crack is glued and is way up at the top so it is covered by the face plate. I could polish it up and send it to you if you'd like? Email me if interested.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg"> ||||reg||4
